-- title:
--   zlib 1.3.1 crc32.c compiled for AArch64, as a placed library
-- statement:
--   The object code of zlib 1.3.1's `crc32.c`, built as zlib ships it by default, as a placed library in the `Arm64` semantics (google-deepmind/code-verification's `Arm64.Trusted`, republished as the `Def_Arm64_*` bundles).
--
--   **The build.** `crc32.c` from the zlib 1.3.1 release tarball (SHA-256 `9a93b2b7…df23`) was compiled with zig cc 0.16.0 for `aarch64-linux-musl` at `-O2`, using the flags of DeepMind's `rust-obj2lean print-cflags`, and with no zlib configuration macros. That is the default braided CRC with $N = 5$ braids of $W = 8$-byte words and the tables pre-computed in `crc32.h`. The object file's SHA-256 is `42c30c7a…3666`. `rust-obj2lean export` turned it into this module. Its byte sidecar is inlined as literal lists, its imports are renamed to the published bundles, and its docstring's account of the upstream build is replaced (the file says so).
--
--   **The library `zlibCrc32Lib`.**
--   - `zlibCrc32Text` is the code block: the 2,824 bytes of `zlibCrc32PlacedCode`, eight function symbols with their offsets (`get_crc_table` at `0x0`, `crc32_z` at `0xc`, `crc32` at `0x7fc`, `crc32_combine64` at `0x804`, `crc32_combine` at `0x8d0`, `crc32_combine_gen64` at `0x99c`, `crc32_combine_gen` at `0xa2c`, `crc32_combine_op` at `0xabc`), and the 17 relocations the linker resolves (table addresses and the branch from `crc32` to `crc32_z`).
--   - `zlibCrc32Data` is the three read-only data objects that crc32.c, lines 142–143, describes as “Tables for byte-wise and braided CRC-32 calculations, and a table of powers of x for combining CRC-32s, all made by make_crc_table().” They are `crc_table` (`zlibCrc32PlacedData0`, 1024 bytes), `crc_braid_table` (`zlibCrc32PlacedData1`, 8192 bytes) and `x2n_table` (`zlibCrc32PlacedData2`, 128 bytes).
--   - The eight functions are the exports.
--
--   The statements quantify over every placement of this library that the `Arm64` model accepts (`Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable`), so no load address or table address is fixed.
-- source:
--   zlib 1.3.1 (J.-l. Gailly and M. Adler, January 22, 2024; https://zlib.net/fossils/zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz, SHA-256 9a93b2b7dfdac77ceba5a558a580e74667dd6fede4585b91eefb60f03b72df23), crc32.c compiled for AArch64 Linux as zlib ships it (zig cc 0.16.0, aarch64-linux-musl, -O2; object SHA-256 42c30c7a…), exported by rust-obj2lean (google-deepmind/code-verification)

